info:
[27 Jul 2013] Prior Park Preparatory School and Prior Park College are pleased to award a discount to parents who have two or more children simultaneously at either of these schools. A discount of 5% will be applied for a second child, 10% for a third child, 15% for a fourth child and 20% for a fifth child. Subject to the points below:
 the sibling discount will be applied in addition to any Scholarship or Exhibition;
 the discount will not be applied in addition to any assistance the family receives in the form of a Bursary. This is because the level of support given by Prior Park in these cases already takes account of all factors including the presence of siblings at other Prior Park schools;
 the discounts will be applied to the fees of the oldest child. That is, if there are two children the older will receive a 5% discount. If there are three children the oldest will receive a 10% discount and the middle child a 5% discount while all three are at Prior Park schools;
 the scheme will be applied regardless of the stage of education within Prior Park, ie, it does not matter whether siblings are in the College, the Preparatory School, providing they are in full-time education;
 the discounts will normally be a percentage of the relevant school fee.

Yes-there are music and academic scholarship
 for sixth form, school will assess from the entrance exams, do not need to do any extra scholarship papers. 
for Year 9- will need to sit scholarship papers in May, there are Maths, English and Science (will need to confirm with school whether they will consider the student for scholarship after the offer.)

- A brand new teaching block is opened for the Humanities subjects in September;
- Our theatre has also been refurbished with a new auditorium to enhance our music, drama and performing arts programme;
- In Oct 2014, our senior boys will have a brand new boarding house with the very latest modern facilities and set within a beautiful wooded area of the campus with far reaching views over the countryside and Bath.
- We shall be launching a new website in end of Sep and will be expanding our International Student information with a new overseas prospectus. (Links to your websites can also be incorporated – please contact Mrs. Angela Dudley-Warde for discussion.)

